(vector (map (:db/id -1)
  (:adr/id "2607199995")
  (:adr/title "introduce kotoba-lang/biomech — biomechanics simulation domain")
  (:adr/status :accepted)
  (:adr/date "2026-07-19")
  (:adr/doc_type "adr")
  (:adr/source-format "edn")
  (:adr/body "# ADR-2607199995: introduce kotoba-lang/biomech — biomechanics simulation domain

- **Status**: accepted (2026-07-19)
- **Related**: repo-wide 3D mandate (CLAUDE.md); kotoba-lang/fea, kotoba-lang/kami-vehicle, kotoba-lang/kami-engine-cfd, kotoba-lang/kami-engine

## Context

2026-07-19 exploration confirmed no dedicated repo in this superproject simulates the human body (muscle / bone / skin / internal organs) in detail. Existing solver assets are real and working, but none carries the biological domain:

- kotoba-lang/character — VRM humanoid skeleton + body mesh (geometry only, no simulation)
- kotoba-lang/fea — linear-static FEM (usable for bone elasticity; zero-dep)
- kotoba-lang/kami-vehicle — BeamNG-grade soft-body XPBD mass-spring (usable for muscle/skin)
- kotoba-lang/kami-engine-cfd — Lattice-Boltzmann CFD D2Q9/D3Q19 (usable for blood/airflow)
- kotoba-lang/kami-engine — DEC voxel PDE (usable for thermal/moisture diffusion)
- com-nvidia-isaac-sim — declares MPM/SPH/FEM in solvers but they are unimplemented stubs

Each solver works in isolation but none owns the tissue-property domain or an integration entry point for whole-body biomechanics.

## Decision

Create kotoba-lang/biomech (public). Phase 1 is zero-dep:

- kotoba.biomech.tissue — tissue-property data layer (cortical/cancellous bone, skeletal muscle, skin, liver, tendon; representative literature values in resources/kami/biomech/tissues.edn)
- kotoba.biomech.osteo — closed-form bone mechanics (Euler-Bernoulli cantilever: tip deflection, max bending stress, second-moment/extreme-fibre section helpers)
- kotoba.biomech.muscle — 1-D lumped mass-spring-damper with an active contractile element (Hill-type reduced to linear; semi-implicit Euler with substepping)

Tissue-property numbers are population-scale representative ranges (NOT patient-specific); each tissue map carries a :source field stating the literature range it was picked from. No fabricated precision.

Phase 2 (separate commits) consumes the existing solvers via :local/root instead of duplicating their numerics:
- fea -> bone FEM (linear-static tet/hex)
- kami-vehicle -> soft-body (muscle/skin large deformation)
- kami-engine-cfd -> blood flow / airflow CFD
- kami-engine DEC -> thermoregulation / moisture

3-D rendering of any sim output uses the kotoba-lang/kami-engine stack (repo-wide 3D mandate). This repo owns the biomech domain + simulation, not rendering.

## Consequences

- A single integration entry point now exists for whole-body biomechanics simulation.
- Phase 1 is zero-dep so the tissue domain + closed-form references stand alone (CI stays simple: clojure -X:test only).
- Phase 2 reuses existing solver repos rather than rebuilding their numerics (consume, do not rebuild).
- Tissue-property data is representative only; README and :source fields disclaim clinical use.
- Phase 2 CI clones each dependency as a sibling (kotoba-lang/host ci.yml pattern).

## Verification

- clojure -X:test — 15 tests / 40 assertions, 0 failures
- clojure -M:lint — 0 errors / 0 warnings
- GitHub repo: https://github.com/kotoba-lang/biomech
- west pin verification: biomech 2929c86 is reachable from kotoba-lang/biomech main (gen-west-manifest --entry biomech verified OK)
- west.yml diff is biomech-only: 5 insertions, 0 other pin changes
")
  (:adr/context "2026-07-19 exploration found no dedicated human-body (muscle/bone/skin/organ) simulation repo in this superproject. Existing solvers (fea, kami-vehicle, kami-engine-cfd, kami-engine DEC) are real and working but carry no biological domain; character provides only geometry. An integration layer + tissue-property domain was missing.")
  (:adr/decision "Create kotoba-lang/biomech (public). Phase 1 zero-dep: kotoba.biomech.tissue (tissue-property data, representative literature values), kotoba.biomech.osteo (Euler-Bernoulli closed-form bone mechanics), kotoba.biomech.muscle (1-D lumped mass-spring-damper with active contractile element). Phase 2 consumes fea/kami-vehicle/kami-engine-cfd/kami-engine via :local/root. 3-D rendering stays in kami-engine (3D mandate). Tissue numbers are population-scale representative ranges with :source provenance, not patient-specific.")
  (:adr/consequences
  (vector "whole-body biomechanics now has a single integration entry point"
   "Phase 1 zero-dep keeps CI simple (clojure -X:test only)"
   "Phase 2 reuses existing solver numerics rather than duplicating them (consume, do not rebuild)"
   "tissue-property data is representative only; README and :source fields disclaim clinical use"
   "Phase 2 CI clones dependencies as siblings (host ci.yml pattern)"))
  (:adr/verification "clojure -X:test: 15 tests / 40 assertions, 0 failures. clojure -M:lint: 0 errors / 0 warnings. GitHub: https://github.com/kotoba-lang/biomech. west pin 2929c86 reachable from kotoba-lang/biomech main (gen-west-manifest --entry biomech OK). west.yml diff biomech-only (5 insertions, 0 other pin changes).")
  (:adr/related (vector "kotoba-lang/fea" "kotoba-lang/kami-vehicle" "kotoba-lang/kami-engine-cfd" "kotoba-lang/kami-engine" "kotoba-lang/character"))))
